<h1>TechEdge Pricing: Complete 2026 Breakdown</h1>

<p>TechEdge is an audience analytics and media planning platform from Fifty5Blue, formerly connected to Kantar Media's software portfolio. It is used by agencies, broadcasters, and advertisers for audience analysis, reach and frequency, campaign evaluation, and cross-media reporting.</p>

<p>The platform is sold as enterprise software. Public monthly plans are not listed, and pricing depends heavily on markets, datasets, modules, and user access.</p>

<h2>Pricing Model</h2>

<p>TechEdge uses a <strong>custom enterprise licensing model</strong>. Cost is likely driven by country or market coverage, the audience datasets included, user count, access to products such as AdvantEdge, API requirements, and support level.</p>

<p>For global networks, the largest cost factor is often data scope rather than software access alone. Audience measurement data rights, local market availability, and integration needs can materially change the quote.</p>

<h2>Pricing Tiers</h2>

<table>
<thead>
<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Pricing</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Single-Market Analytics</td><td>Custom quote</td><td>Teams focused on one country or audience dataset</td></tr>
<tr><td>Multi-Market Planning</td><td>Custom quote</td><td>Agencies and broadcasters comparing markets or platforms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Enterprise Data Integration</td><td>Custom quote</td><td>Organizations needing APIs, automation, and proprietary workflow integration</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>What's Included</h2>

<p>Packages can include audience analysis, reach and frequency planning, campaign evaluation, cross-media reporting, local measurement datasets, advanced audience tools, and API access. The exact package depends on licensed markets and data sources.</p>

<p>Buyers should confirm whether panel data, big data, digital datasets, clean room workflows, and API access are included in the base contract or priced as add-ons.</p>

<h2>Total Cost of Ownership</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Data rights:</strong> Licensed audience datasets can be a major cost driver.</li>
<li><strong>Market coverage:</strong> Multi-country teams should expect broader scoping than single-market buyers.</li>
<li><strong>Integrations:</strong> APIs and workflow automation can add implementation work.</li>
<li><strong>Training:</strong> Planning and research teams may need onboarding for local measurement conventions.</li>
<li><strong>Governance:</strong> Global teams need consistent definitions for targets, platforms, and campaign reporting.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who It's Best For / Not For</h2>

<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Agencies, broadcasters, and advertisers that need professional audience analysis, reach-frequency workflows, and market-specific measurement data.</p>

<p><strong>Not ideal for:</strong> Teams looking for low-cost media plan presentation software, paid media dashboards, or simple campaign pacing tools.</p>

<h2>Alternatives</h2>

<ul>
<li>Nielsen Ad Intel — Competitive ad intelligence and media spend context.</li>
<li>Kantar — Media intelligence, audience measurement, and research services.</li>
<li>iSpot.tv — TV and video measurement with outcome analytics.</li>
<li>Vivvix — Competitive advertising intelligence from the former Kantar/Ad Intel ecosystem.</li>
<li>Pathmatics — Digital advertising intelligence and spend estimates.</li>
</ul>

<p>See the full <a href="/techedge/alternatives">TechEdge alternatives</a> page for a broader comparison.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Does TechEdge publish pricing?</h3>
<p>No. TechEdge pricing is custom-quoted and depends on markets, datasets, modules, and users.</p>

<h3>Is TechEdge priced by market?</h3>
<p>Market and data coverage are likely major factors. Audience measurement platforms often price differently for single-market, regional, and global access.</p>

<h3>Is TechEdge the same as Kantar?</h3>
<p>TechEdge is associated with Fifty5Blue's audience analytics software portfolio. The broader Kantar and former Kantar Media ecosystem includes multiple measurement and intelligence products.</p>

<h3>Does TechEdge include reach and frequency planning?</h3>
<p>Yes. Reach and frequency analysis is a core use case, including the AdvantEdge engine described in public product materials.</p>

<h3>What should buyers ask in a demo?</h3>
<p>Ask which datasets are included, how local market data is licensed, how fast R&F calculations run on your data, and whether exports or APIs fit your workflow.</p>

